# ── Public Notice Management — monorepo env layout ────────────────────
# This repo has NO shared/global .env — each app loads its own env file
# from its own directory. Copy the per-app example to the real file and
# fill in your values. Real env files are gitignored; never commit secrets.
#
# ┌─────────┬───────────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────┐
# │ App     │ Copy template                 │ Real file (gitignored)   │
# ├─────────┼───────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────┤
# │ web     │ apps/web/.env.example         │ apps/web/.env.local      │
# │ api     │ apps/api/.env.example         │ apps/api/.env            │
# │ ai      │ apps/ai/.env.example          │ apps/ai/.env             │
# └─────────┴───────────────────────────────┴──────────────────────────┘
#
# Ports: web :3000 · api :5005 · ai :8000
#
# Key cross-app links (see each app's .env.example for the full list):
#   - apps/api/.env  → DATABASE_URL, JWT_SECRET, GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID,
#                      ADMIN_EMAILS, AI_SERVICE_URL, EVOLUTION_*
#   - apps/web/.env.local → NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL (must point at the API),
#                      NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID (must MATCH the API's)
#   - apps/ai/.env    → QDRANT_URL, GEMINI_API_KEY, GROQ_API_KEY(S),
#                      CORS_ORIGINS (must include http://localhost:3000)
#
# Global / non-app settings that apply to everyone (e.g. WEB_ORIGIN, CORS)
# live in the app that enforces them — not at the repo root.
